# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings. git's core.autocrlf defaults to true on
# Windows, and a CRLF-converted snap.sh dies before it runs a single command:
#   snap.sh: line 29: $'\r': command not found
#   snap.sh: line 30: set: pipefail: invalid option name
# (Reported from the field 2026-08-20.) bash cannot self-diagnose this -- it is
# already dead -- so the only real defence is to never let the conversion happen.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch them.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
